# Naming vocabulary (Teensy looper)

Use with global **`naming-and-terminology`**: clear **action + scope** (ideal two words; longer when needed for completeness), no abbreviations, reuse terms below.

Read before M8+ edit storage, OpenSpec **`m8-rename`** then **`m8-edit`**, or timeline refactors.

## Scope words (Loop slot)

| Scope | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **Loop** | Slot container |
| **Capture** | Live record/overdub buffer (was `CaptureLayer`) |
| **Take** | Committed capture — Record or Overdub (was `Epoch`) |
| **Edit** | One committed `saveEdit` unit in `edits[]` |
| **EditChange** | One atomic change inside an **Edit** |
| **pass** | One bounded capture or edit stretch ending in commit (see **Pass types** below) |

## Pass types (audio/MIDI time)

Umbrella term for a single committed stretch on the loop timeline:

| Pass | Ends with | Global undo (when applicable) |
|------|-----------|-------------------------------|
| **record pass** | `commitTake()` → Record **Take** | **TakeCommitted** |
| **overdub pass** | `commitTake()` → Overdub **Take** | **TakeCommitted** |
| **edit pass** | `closeNoteEditPass()` (boundary flush) | **NoteEditSessionCommitted** |

An **edit pass** is a sub-period inside **NoteEditSession** between overdub-while-editing or
note-edit exit boundaries. Each **Edit** stores `editPassIndex` (legacy field name: `spanIndex`).

**Do not** use **pass** for: moving note tick range (**moving note range** on focus), or single-note **focus**
lifecycle.

## Types and ids

| Name | Role |
|------|------|
| **EditChangeType** | Enum of change types |
| **TakeType** | Record \| Overdub (was `EpochKind`) |
| **EditId** | Stable id per **Edit** |
| **NoteRef** | Stable note target in an **EditChange** |

