## UI rename

- `class EditState` → **`EditNoteState`** (note-edit FSM base)
- **`EditState`** on struct **Edit** = Active \| Disabled (parallel **TakeState**)

## Note edit overlap (moving note + overlap notes)

Pair used during live note edit (move / length / pitch). **Overlap note** is the umbrella;
qualifiers below are sub-definitions — not separate top-level nouns.

| Term | Role |
|------|------|
| **moving note** | Note being edited (`MovingNoteIdentity`; fader-1 selection) |
| **overlap note** | Any other note the moving note edit affects (hide, shorten, restore) |
| **OverlapNote** | One tracked overlap note on **focus** (target: replaces `DeletedNote`) |
| **overlapNotes** | Collection on **focus** — **impacted overlap notes only** (not `baselineMap`) |
| **OverlapNoteStoreState** | **Visible** \| **Hidden** \| **Shortened** on each **OverlapNote** |

**Relationship** (what kind of overlap note):

| Qualifier | Meaning |
|-----------|---------|
| **overlapping** | Ranges intersect the moving note’s start/end/pitch gate |
| **inner** | Wholly inside the moving note **range** (focus `movingNoteRange`) |
| **adjacent** | Shares a boundary tick (lane merge) |
| **contained** | Fully inside moving note range (matches “completely contained note” logs) |

**Store state** (on each **OverlapNote** entry):

| State | Meaning |
|-------|---------|
| **hidden** | Note pair removed from session store |
| **shortened** | Head or tail cut; still in store |
| **visible** | Present in store (normal or after restore) |

Do **not** use **victim**, **covered** (use **hidden**), **neighbor** / **neighbor note** (use
**overlap note**), **ledger** (overlap tracking — use **overlapNotes**; playback uses
**ActiveNoteLedger**), **flat** in new names (use **loop MIDI events**, **session store events**,
or **Takes + Edits replay**), **footprint** (use **moving note range** on focus), **span** (use
**edit pass**), **layer** for edit batches (use **edit pass**; **layer** = Take/overdub performance), new abbreviations.

## Words to avoid for new names

**segment**, **gesture**, **working**, **EditOp**, **published** (use **committed**), storing edits as Takes, **victim**, **covered** (use **hidden**), **neighbor** / **neighbor note** (use **overlap note**), **ledger** for overlap scratch (use **overlapNotes**), **flat** in new identifiers (use scope: **loop MIDI events**, **session store events**, **Takes + Edits replay**), **footprint** (use **moving note range** on **NoteEditFocus**), **span** (use **edit pass**), **layer** for edit batches (use **edit pass**; **layer** = Take/overdub performance), new abbreviations. Prefer **Type** over **Kind** for new enums when the repo uses **Type** elsewhere.

Ask before introducing a **new domain noun** or session type name not listed above.

## Identifier rules (functions, types, OpenSpec)

Follow global **`naming-and-terminology`**. In this repo specifically:

1. **Action + scope** — name what the code *does* and *what it applies to* (e.g. `commitTake`, `filterSelectableDisplayNotes`, `rebuildNoteEditFocusFromStore`). Two words minimum when possible; longer when needed for clarity.
2. **Reuse domain nouns** from this file — **Take**, **Edit**, **NoteEditSession**, **DisplayNote**, **NoteRef**, **overlap note**, **select navigation** (`SelectNavigation`, `SelectNavSlot`), **focus**, **moving note**.
3. **No new top-level nouns** (types, modules, capability names) without **explicit user approval** — propose term, why existing words fail, one-sentence rationale; do not implement until agreed.
4. **No abbreviations** in new identifiers. **No metaphor imports** — avoid **audible**, **view**, **inventory**, **projection**, **ledger**, **wire**, **golden** unless already listed above.
5. **Describe, don’t invent** — if the object already has a name, use it in prose (e.g. “reconstruct **DisplayNote** list from **NoteEditSession.store**”) instead of coining a synonym type (`audibleNotes`, `sessionView`).

### Note edit — read path (no new module noun)

| Need | Use | Avoid |
|------|-----|-------|
| MIDI pairs during edit | **NoteEditSession.store** / `editAwareMidiEvents()` | “audible”, “live layer” |
| Reconstructed notes | **`NoteUtils::reconstructNotes`** → **`DisplayNote`** | `audibleNotes`, `sessionNotes` |
| Fader-1 + display list excluding **Hidden** overlap | **`filterSelectableDisplayNotes`** (action + object) | `NoteEditSessionView`, `selectableNotes()` as a type |
| Bracket / delete target | **`NoteRef`** + select navigation index | cache index without **NoteRef** |

When a helper is needed, prefer adding it on **`NoteEditFocus`** or **`SelectNavigation`** — not a new `*View` / `*Inventory` type unless the user approves the name.
